From e85501de30f421fd0c3acbd9dca61b7e4e4c68a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:47:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(kanban): change-proportional annotation holder
 (card B)

Card B of design t_01a1d563324d7e8e (task t_01a1d59e531bd0a4). The serve that holds
the kanban-annotation lease spent ~30% of a core in _holder_refresh: the exact
activity fingerprint moves in ~65% of 2 s passes, and most of that movement is
liveness churn (rf2: 67% of changed replica task rows activity-only).

What changes
1. Narrow holder/display key (kanban_annotation_narrow + reader/semantic/ledger/
   dependencies). Per origin scope: liveness-normalized semantic tokens of replica
   rows linking the origin, ledger-bound owners and every same (board, id)
   publisher; the scoped origin-ledger snapshot plus raw owner-current bits;
   gateway info/last_ok as 180 s buckets plus offline; own boards, shadows and
   waiting inputs exact. activity_at/activity_kind and a VALID observation's
   task_hash restamp never move it. Read errors return None = moved (exact
   fallback); strict callers (task APIs, closeout, default _remote_links) keep
   the exact _links_fingerprint path.
   DependencySelector is incremental (TaskTokens reports the changed keys), the
   ledger snapshot is memoized on the same connection's data_version, and the
   current-match verdict is cached per immutable row object.
2. 10 s per-scope floor after an input-moved refresh; 2 s probe and 20 s forced
   renewal unchanged. An unchanged narrow key re-stamps the header's verified_at.
3. Split host copy: small always-rewritten header (fingerprint, read_at, parts
   digest, mutation ack, display identity, narrow key) + content-addressed body
   written only when the parts change (bounded current+previous retention).
4. Own-mutation kick (R10): foreground Kanban tool/HTTP/hosted-ASGI writes cue
   the scope after the outer COMMIT; post_llm_call callbacks with registered
   waiting sources cue conservatively. The cue is acknowledged only in the same
   atomic header as a forced read that started after it.
5. Display adoption: sidebar/stamps/tree adopt a <=12 s host copy (verified_at
   counts) before exact probes; strict adopt stays exact. B owns the tree route's
   inline refresh (C3).

Proof
- RED->GREEN suites: host split, holder floor, holder narrow, narrow key, reader,
  semantic tokens, ledger snapshot/current, dependencies, incremental
  selector (12-seed equivalence vs full scan), own-commit + mutation routes,
  closeout cue, display adoption. Mutants: incremental touched-seed check
  (14 fail), postcommit flush (13 fail), invalid-hash normalization, closeout
  inputs prime.
- scripts/benchmark_kanban_annotation_holder.py: 10k/20k/40k replica tiers,
  rf2 churn mix, checkpointed WAL and 440 MB WAL. Liveness-only churn never
  moves the key. Narrow key mean 7.6/14.0/32.5 ms (WAL size no effect).
  C2 census replay (default scope, 300 s): 28 refreshes vs 98 for today's rule;
  modelled holder 6.0% vs 18.5% at the P1 post-C 553.6 ms/refresh.
- Budget: NOT met by narrowing alone. The forced 20 s renewal at the measured
  per-refresh cost is 2.77% by itself, above the 2.4% holder budget; the
  overrun is reported through P1, not waived.
